  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>Offline Expense Tracker-Budget (“the app”) is published by SM Technologies (“we”, “us”). This policy explains how the app handles your information.</p>

  <h2>Information the app stores</h2>
  <p>The app stores the information you type into it: accounts, categories, transactions (amounts, dates, notes), budgets, loans and repayments, repeating entries, and your settings such as language, currency and theme.</p>
  <p>This information is kept only in the app’s private storage on your device. It is never sent to us or to any server. We cannot see it, and we have no copy of it.</p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>None. The app does not collect, transmit or sell any personal or usage data. It contains no advertising, analytics, crash-reporting or tracking software, and it does not use an advertising ID.</p>

  <h2>Internet and permissions</h2>
  <p>The app does not request internet access, so it cannot send data off your device. It does not access your location, contacts, camera, microphone, photos, phone number or other accounts.</p>

  <h2>Files you choose to create</h2>
  <p>You can export your records as a CSV or PDF file, or create a backup file. These files are created only when you ask for them, and are handed to Android’s share sheet. Where they go next (for example a cloud drive, email or a messaging app) is your choice, and is covered by that service’s own privacy policy.</p>
  <p>Backup files are not encrypted. Keep them as safely as you would keep a bank statement.</p>

  <h2>Device backups</h2>
  <p>The app tells Android not to include its data in automatic cloud backups or device-to-device transfers. To move your data to a new phone, create a backup file in the app and restore it on the new phone.</p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>You can delete all data at any time in the app under <em>Settings → Erase all data</em>. Uninstalling the app also deletes everything it stored. Files you exported or backed up are separate; delete them wherever you saved them.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>The app is intended for adults. It does not collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>Because your data never leaves your device, its safety depends on your device’s own protection. We recommend using a screen lock on your phone.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If the app’s handling of data ever changes, for example if an optional sync feature is added, we will update this page and change the effective date above before that change reaches you.</p>

